        "content_text": "<a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/\">The Greatest Music </a> squashes many well-known-and-pored-over <a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/lists\">\"Greatest 500 [Albums/Songs/Artists] of [A Certain Time Period]\" lists</a> through <a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/rankings\">an algorithmic system</a> of <a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/songs/lists/22\">weights</a> and <a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/albums/lists/4\">pulleys</a>, and out comes the <a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/songs?page=51\">One True List</a> (<a href=\"https://thegreatestmusic.org/albums/1902-1954\"><em>e.g., a custom 1902&#8211;1954 LPs edition</em></a>)</em>. <small><em>{cue choir and fanfare}</em></small> <a href=\"https://github.com/ssherman/weighted_list_rank\">Code Junkies can see how the sausage is made here.</a>",
