        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/Law-proposed-to-ban-AI-companies-from-selling-your-health-data.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">People commonly disclose all kinds of personal data to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/artificial-intelligence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI</a> chatbots, including the highly inadvisable practice of asking them for <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/apple-health/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">health</a> advice. In addition to the grave medical dangers of obtaining inaccurate advice, users are also running significant <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/privacy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">privacy</a> risks.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most AI chatbots have terms and conditions that allow any of your conversations with them to be used as training data, and often app terms that allow data to be collated and sold. Democrats now propose to update a privacy law to prevent the sale of health data …</p>",
